note The io-map crate's surface: the boundary between the domain Map and the .codemap directory. Callers (the codemap binary, cli's diff, the GUI) make a MapStore for a root, load, resolve and edit the Map in domain, then save; MapStore::base reads a revision's map for diff. The crate guarantees that rendering is deterministic, so an unchanged path saves to identical bytes, that it never writes a path whose text is what it read or last wrote, and that every fault comes back as a value naming the file or revision and line, never a panic and never a partial map. The format and the load and save walk are the map-file path.

